{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "DGLD",
  "name": "DGLD transferFrom returns true without moving tokens, minting unbacked DGLD on Base",
  "summary": "DGLDToken.transferFrom (inherited by DGLDTokenV2 0xae84fb58 behind the DGLD proxy 0xa9299c29) moves only min(balanceOf(from), amount), skips the transfer entirely when the sender holds nothing, and returns true either way. Base's L1StandardBridge depositERC20 pulls the deposit with safeTransferFrom and then tells Base to mint the full requested amount of the L2 token 0xd02f50e1, so a depositor with no DGLD gets DGLD minted on Base for free. The attacker 0x40963a79, after a real 0.001 DGLD test deposit, deposited 0.002 DGLD it did not hold in the anchor; it and four other depositors then bridged 100 to 100M phantom DGLD and sold it into Base's DGLD pools for 162,863 USDC, 24,495 USDT and 4.05 ETH.",
